In Ladybird, a floated table row group is a block float now, which
table fixup wraps in an anonymous row and cell like any other non-table
child of a table, while an absolutely positioned one stays a direct
child of the table. All three engines blockify a float first: Blink in
StyleAdjuster::AdjustComputedStyle(), with EquivalentBlockDisplay(),
WebKit in Style::Adjuster::adjust(), with blockified(), and Gecko in
StyleAdjuster::blockify_if_necessary(). Each then wraps the resulting
block in anonymous table parts: Blink in LayoutObject::AddChild(),
whose RequiresAnonymousTableWrappers() asks only for real table parts,
WebKit in RenderTreeBuilder::Table::findOrCreateParentForChild(), which
creates an anonymous section, and Gecko in nsCSSFrameConstructor::
CreateNeededPseudoContainers(). Chrome 158, Firefox 151 and WebKit 26.5
all render the rows of a floated tbody, thead or tr that way.
